 "https://github.com/cli/cli/pull/15095#pullrequestreview-5958177209": {
  "body": "<!-- ccr-overview-v2 -->\n\n### \ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look\n\nThe version and checksum edits are consistent, but missing upstream v2.1.1 changes and unavailable build/CI validation leave dependency compatibility and terminal-rendering behavior unconfirmed.\n\n**No open issues** \ud83c\udf89\n\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n\nUpdates GitHub CLI\u2019s Lip Gloss terminal-styling dependency from v2.1.0 to v2.1.1.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Bumps the dependency version in `go.mod`.\n- Replaces the module and `go.mod` checksums in `go.sum` for the new version.\n\n| File | Description |\r\n| ---- | ----------- |\r\n| go.sum | Updates Lip Gloss checksums to v2.1.1. |\r\n| go.mod | Requires Lip Gloss v2.1.1 instead of v2.1.0. |\n</details>\n\n<sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub>",
  "bodyHTML": "\n<h3 dir=\"auto\">\ud83d\udd35 Needs a closer look</h3>\n<p dir=\"auto\">The version and checksum edits are consistent, but missing upstream v2.1.1 changes and unavailable build/CI validation leave dependency compatibility and terminal-rendering behavior unconfirmed.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>No open issues</strong> \ud83c\udf89</p>\n<details>\n<summary><strong>What changed in this PR</strong></summary>\n<p dir=\"auto\">Updates GitHub CLI\u2019s Lip Gloss terminal-styling dependency from v2.1.0 to v2.1.1.</p>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><strong>Changes:</strong></p>\n<ul dir=\"auto\">\n<li>Bumps the dependency version in <code class=\"notranslate\">go.mod</code>.</li>\n<li>Replaces the module and <code class=\"notranslate\">go.mod</code> checksums in <code class=\"notranslate\">go.sum</code> for the new version.</li>\n</ul>\n<markdown-accessiblity-table><table role=\"table\">\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>File</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td>go.sum</td>\n<td>Updates Lip Gloss checksums to v2.1.1.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>go.mod</td>\n<td>Requires Lip Gloss v2.1.1 instead of v2.1.0.</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></markdown-accessiblity-table>\n</details>\n<p dir=\"auto\"><sub>Review effort: Balanced</sub></p>"
 },
 "https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633#issuecomment-7026446245": {
  "body": "This was a bug that came up while I was managing my own homepage, so I\r\ndidn\u2019t fully understand the severity of security issues. I should have\r\nlooked into it more before acting, and I apologize again. Basically, I\r\ndon\u2019t do much community or maintenance work, and this was simply because I\r\nwanted to quickly find and fix a problem that occurred on my homepage. I\u2019ve\r\ndeleted the PR and will report it privately instead.\r\n\r\n2026\ub144 11\uc6d4 20\uc77c (\uae08) \uc624\uc804 9:26, Jordan Harband ***@***.***>\ub2d8\uc774 \uc791\uc131:\r\n\r\n> *ljharb* left a comment (nodejs/node#67633)\r\n> <https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633#issuecomment-7026294073>\r\n>\r\n> Reporting a potential vulnerability publicly is VERY irresponsible and\r\n> contradicts the security policy, which explicitly tells you what to do in\r\n> the case HackerOne won't accept your report.\r\n>\r\n> Separately, once you're running that untrusted code, which has filesystem\r\n> access, you're already screwed, and no further capability is relevant.\r\n>\r\n> \u2014\r\n> Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\r\n> <https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633?email_source=notifications&email_token=REDACTED#issuecomment-7026294073>,\r\n> or unsubscribe\r\n> <https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/REDACTED>\r\n> .\r\n> You are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID:\r\n> <nodejs/node/issues/67633/7026294073 ***@***.***>\r\n>\r\n",
  "bodyHTML": "<div class=\"email-fragment\">This was a bug that came up while I was managing my own homepage, so I\ndidn\u2019t fully understand the severity of security issues. I should have\nlooked into it more before acting, and I apologize again. Basically, I\ndon\u2019t do much community or maintenance work, and this was simply because I\nwanted to quickly find and fix a problem that occurred on my homepage. I\u2019ve\ndeleted the PR and will report it privately instead.\n\n2026\ub144 11\uc6d4 20\uc77c (\uae08) \uc624\uc804 9:26, Jordan Harband ***@***.***&gt;\ub2d8\uc774 \uc791\uc131:</div>\n<span class=\"email-hidden-toggle\"><a href=\"#\">\u2026</a></span><div class=\"email-hidden-reply\">\n<div class=\"email-quoted-reply\"> *ljharb* left a comment (<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6501311895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633\" href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633\">nodejs/node#67633</a>)\n &lt;<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6501311895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633\" href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633#issuecomment-7026294073\">#67633 (comment)</a>&gt;\n\n Reporting a potential vulnerability publicly is VERY irresponsible and\n contradicts the security policy, which explicitly tells you what to do in\n the case HackerOne won't accept your report.\n\n Separately, once you're running that untrusted code, which has filesystem\n access, you're already screwed, and no further capability is relevant.\n\n \u2014\n Reply to this email directly, view it on GitHub\n &lt;<a class=\"issue-link js-issue-link\" data-error-text=\"Failed to load title\" data-id=\"6501311895\" data-permission-text=\"Title is private\" data-url=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633\" href=\"https://github.com/nodejs/node/issues/67633\">#67633</a>?email_source=notifications&amp;email_token=REDACTED#issuecomment-7026294073&gt;,\n or unsubscribe\n &lt;<a href=\"https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/REDACTED\">https://github.com/notifications/unsubscribe-auth/REDACTED</a>&gt;\n .\n You are receiving this because you authored the thread.Message ID:\n &lt;nodejs/node/issues/67633/7026294073 ***@***.***&gt;\n</div>\n<div class=\"email-fragment\"></div>\n</div>"
